---
title: Grok Build
id: grok-build-adapter
order: 15
description: "Use xAI's Grok Build coding agent as a chat backend in TanStack AI — a sandbox harness that runs the grok CLI against a real workspace, with tool bridging via @tanstack/ai-grok-build."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - grok
  - grok build
  - xai
  - harness
  - agent
  - coding agent
  - adapter
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Grok Build adapter runs xAI's "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok Build"}]},{"type":"text","value":" coding agent as a chat backend.\nUnlike HTTP provider adapters, this is a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"harness adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Grok Build runs\nits own agent loop and executes its own tools — shell commands, file edits,\nsearch — by spawning the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok"},{"type":"text","value":" CLI "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"inside a sandbox"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call runs\none full harness turn; the harness's tool activity streams back as\nalready-resolved tool-call events your UI can render."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requires a sandbox."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build"},{"type":"text","value":" declares "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires: [SandboxCapability]"},{"type":"text","value":",\nso "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" errors at the call site unless you provide a sandbox with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" middleware. The sandbox — your laptop, a Docker container,\nor a cloud VM — is the filesystem and safety boundary the agent runs in. See\nthe "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandboxes overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full picture."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You also need a sandbox provider (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker"},{"type":"text","value":") and the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok"},{"type":"text","value":" CLI available inside the sandbox image."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"authentication","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authentication"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your laptop can already have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok login"},{"type":"text","value":". A CI runner only has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":".\nBoth can use the same sandbox provider. The default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":".\nSet "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" when you want "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok login"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { grokBuildText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\"\n\ngrokBuildText(\"composer-2.5\")\ngrokBuildText(\"composer-2.5\", { authMode: \"host\" })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default): inject "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" and authenticate with it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":": skip ACP "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authenticate"},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok login"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not inject\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" into that process."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The two modes list the model under slightly different ids. The adapter maps\nthe short alias for you (see "},{"type":"link","href":"#models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\nimport { messages, threadId } from './chat-context'\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'grok-build-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n    setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n    secrets: createSecrets({ XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '' }),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  threadId,\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok Build accepts any xAI model id its backend supports; the known ids get\nautocomplete (any string is allowed):"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notes"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The short alias. With a grok.com browser login the CLI lists it under this name."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build-0.1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The fully-qualified id the CLI lists when authenticated with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"composer-2.5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Also runnable through the Grok Build harness."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass any of these to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokBuildText(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" — the adapter resolves "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build"},{"type":"text","value":" to\nthe CLI's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build-0.1"},{"type":"text","value":" automatically, so the same code works under both auth\nmodes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter config (second argument to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokBuildText"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cwd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Working directory inside the sandbox. Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/workspace"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokExecutable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path/name of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok"},{"type":"text","value":" executable inside the sandbox. Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"env"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extra environment variables for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok"},{"type":"text","value":" process inside the sandbox."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitDiff"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emit a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file.changed"},{"type":"text","value":" CUSTOM event with the working-tree "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff"},{"type":"text","value":" after the run. Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"protocol"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness wire protocol: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'acp'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'streaming-json'"},{"type":"text","value":". Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'acp'"},{"type":"text","value":". A durable sandbox run with no protocol set uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'streaming-json'"},{"type":"text","value":" so the run can journal."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default) uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok login"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMethodId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit ACP auth method. Wins over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"extraArgs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extra raw CLI flags appended verbatim (advanced)."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-call overrides go through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessionId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resume an existing Grok Build session (see below)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cwd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-call override of the harness working directory."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTurns"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-call cap on the number of harness turns."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"protocol"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-call override of the harness wire protocol."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":". Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMethodId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-call ACP auth method. Wins over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"stateful-sessions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stateful Sessions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok Build sessions are stateful — the harness keeps the working context (files\nread, commands run, conclusions reached) between turns. The adapter surfaces the\nsession id of every fresh run as a custom stream event named\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":"; thread it back via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.sessionId"},{"type":"text","value":" to resume.\nWhen resuming, only the latest user message is sent — the harness already holds\nthe prior context."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, chatParamsFromRequest, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const sessionId =\n    typeof params.forwardedProps.sessionId === 'string'\n      ? params.forwardedProps.sessionId\n      : undefined\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n    modelOptions: { sessionId },\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two kinds of tools flow through this adapter:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in harness tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are executed by Grok Build itself (shell, file\nedits, search) and stream back as tool-call events with results already\nattached. Your code never executes them."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your TanStack tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are bridged "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"into"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the harness over an authenticated\nMCP tool-proxy: define them with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition().server()"},{"type":"text","value":" and pass them to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ tools })"},{"type":"text","value":". Tool-call events come back under the names you registered.\nBecause the harness runs in a sandbox, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor how the bridge reaches your host across providers (local/Docker vs cloud)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-side and approval-gated tools are not supported"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the harness runs\ntools inside a live process and can't pause across an HTTP round-trip. A tool\nwithout a server "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute()"},{"type":"text","value":" (or marked "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsApproval"},{"type":"text","value":") fails fast; run those\nwith a regular provider adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"durable-runs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Durable runs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A durable sandbox run (you pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"durability"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":")\njournals the agent output so a later request can take the run over. ACP does\nnot journal. When durability is wired and you do not set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"protocol"},{"type":"text","value":", the\nadapter uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'streaming-json'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"protocol: 'acp'"},{"type":"text","value":" only when you want ACP on that call. A fresh ACP run\nwith durability wired logs a warning. An attach against ACP throws\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DurableAttachNotSupportedError"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"headless-ndjson-flags","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Headless NDJSON flags"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'streaming-json'"},{"type":"text","value":" path with auto-approve, the adapter adds\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--always-approve --no-plan --no-auto-update"},{"type":"text","value":". Those flags keep Plan Mode and\nthe CLI update check from blocking a headless run."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"structured-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured Output"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":". Grok Build has no native schema flag. The adapter adds the JSON Schema to the prompt (ACP and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streaming-json"},{"type":"text","value":") and parses the last assistant text. Tool activity still streams. The object arrives as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { grokBuildText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\"\nimport { defineSandbox, withSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n})\n\nconst report = await chat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText(\"grok-build\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Review this repo.\" }],\n  outputSchema: Report,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n\nreport.summary","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This path parses JSON from the last assistant message. If extract-only is the job, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-grok"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the client, pass the same schema to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" and read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"final"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial"},{"type":"text","value":" stays empty until the end."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nfunction ReportView() {\n  const { final, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/repo-report\"),\n    outputSchema: Report,\n  })\n\n  if (isLoading) return <p>The agent is inspecting the repo.</p>\n  if (!final) return null\n  return <p>{final.summary}</p>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full walkthrough, including the client: "},{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/harnesses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Agents"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limitations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limitations"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requires a sandbox."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Always run it under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox(...)"},{"type":"text","value":"; see the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandboxes overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-only (Node)."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The harness spawns the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok"},{"type":"text","value":" CLI in a sandbox."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The harness owns the agent loop."}]},{"type":"text","value":" TanStack's agent-loop strategies and\nper-iteration middleware don't apply inside a harness turn."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No sampling controls."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":"-style options don't exist here."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cold starts."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Each call runs a full harness turn; expect higher first-token\nlatency than HTTP adapters."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"authentication","text":"Authentication","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"models","text":"Models","level":2},{"id":"configuration","text":"Configuration","level":2},{"id":"stateful-sessions","text":"Stateful Sessions","level":2},{"id":"tools","text":"Tools","level":2},{"id":"durable-runs","text":"Durable runs","level":2},{"id":"headless-ndjson-flags","text":"Headless NDJSON flags","level":2},{"id":"structured-output","text":"Structured Output","level":2},{"id":"limitations","text":"Limitations","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe Grok Build adapter runs xAI's **Grok Build** coding agent as a chat backend.\nUnlike HTTP provider adapters, this is a **harness adapter**: Grok Build runs\nits own agent loop and executes its own tools — shell commands, file edits,\nsearch — by spawning the `grok` CLI **inside a sandbox**. Each `chat()` call runs\none full harness turn; the harness's tool activity streams back as\nalready-resolved tool-call events your UI can render.\n\n> **Requires a sandbox.** `grok-build` declares `requires: [SandboxCapability]`,\n> so `chat()` errors at the call site unless you provide a sandbox with\n> `withSandbox(...)` middleware. The sandbox — your laptop, a Docker container,\n> or a cloud VM — is the filesystem and safety boundary the agent runs in. See\n> the [Sandboxes overview](../sandbox/overview) for the full picture.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nvue: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\npreact: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nangular: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\noctane: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nYou also need a sandbox provider (e.g. `@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker`) and the\n`grok` CLI available inside the sandbox image.\n\n## Authentication\n\nYour laptop can already have `grok login`. A CI runner only has `XAI_API_KEY`.\nBoth can use the same sandbox provider. The default `authMode` is `'api-key'`.\nSet `'host'` when you want `grok login`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth).\n\n```ts\nimport { grokBuildText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\"\n\ngrokBuildText(\"composer-2.5\")\ngrokBuildText(\"composer-2.5\", { authMode: \"host\" })\n```\n\n- `'api-key'` (default): inject `XAI_API_KEY` and authenticate with it.\n- `'host'`: skip ACP `authenticate`. Use `grok login`. Do not inject\n  `XAI_API_KEY` into that process.\n\nThe two modes list the model under slightly different ids. The adapter maps\nthe short alias for you (see [Models](#models)).\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\nimport { messages, threadId } from './chat-context'\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'grok-build-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n    setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n    secrets: createSecrets({ XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '' }),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  threadId,\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\n## Models\n\nGrok Build accepts any xAI model id its backend supports; the known ids get\nautocomplete (any string is allowed):\n\n| Model id | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| `grok-build` | The short alias. With a grok.com browser login the CLI lists it under this name. |\n| `grok-build-0.1` | The fully-qualified id the CLI lists when authenticated with `XAI_API_KEY`. |\n| `composer-2.5` | Also runnable through the Grok Build harness. |\n\nPass any of these to `grokBuildText(...)` — the adapter resolves `grok-build` to\nthe CLI's `grok-build-0.1` automatically, so the same code works under both auth\nmodes.\n\n## Configuration\n\nAdapter config (second argument to `grokBuildText`):\n\n| Option           | Description                                                                 |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cwd`            | Working directory inside the sandbox. Defaults to `/workspace`.             |\n| `grokExecutable` | Path/name of the `grok` executable inside the sandbox. Defaults to `grok`.  |\n| `env`            | Extra environment variables for the `grok` process inside the sandbox.      |\n| `emitDiff`       | Emit a `file.changed` CUSTOM event with the working-tree `git diff` after the run. Defaults to `true`. |\n| `protocol`       | Harness wire protocol: `'acp'` or `'streaming-json'`. Defaults to `'acp'`. A durable sandbox run with no protocol set uses `'streaming-json'` so the run can journal. |\n| `authMode`       | `'api-key'` (default) uses `XAI_API_KEY`. `'host'` uses `grok login`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth). |\n| `authMethodId`   | Explicit ACP auth method. Wins over `authMode`.                             |\n| `extraArgs`      | Extra raw CLI flags appended verbatim (advanced).                           |\n\nPer-call overrides go through `modelOptions`:\n\n| `modelOptions`  | Description                                                  |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `sessionId`     | Resume an existing Grok Build session (see below).           |\n| `cwd`           | Per-call override of the harness working directory.          |\n| `maxTurns`      | Per-call cap on the number of harness turns.                 |\n| `protocol`      | Per-call override of the harness wire protocol.              |\n| `authMode`      | Per-call `'host'` or `'api-key'`. Default `'api-key'`.       |\n| `authMethodId`  | Per-call ACP auth method. Wins over `authMode`.              |\n\n## Stateful Sessions\n\nGrok Build sessions are stateful — the harness keeps the working context (files\nread, commands run, conclusions reached) between turns. The adapter surfaces the\nsession id of every fresh run as a custom stream event named\n`grok-build.session-id`; thread it back via `modelOptions.sessionId` to resume.\nWhen resuming, only the latest user message is sent — the harness already holds\nthe prior context.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat, chatParamsFromRequest, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const sessionId =\n    typeof params.forwardedProps.sessionId === 'string'\n      ? params.forwardedProps.sessionId\n      : undefined\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n    modelOptions: { sessionId },\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n## Tools\n\nTwo kinds of tools flow through this adapter:\n\n1. **Built-in harness tools** are executed by Grok Build itself (shell, file\n   edits, search) and stream back as tool-call events with results already\n   attached. Your code never executes them.\n2. **Your TanStack tools** are bridged *into* the harness over an authenticated\n   MCP tool-proxy: define them with `toolDefinition().server()` and pass them to\n   `chat({ tools })`. Tool-call events come back under the names you registered.\n   Because the harness runs in a sandbox, see [Sandbox tools](../sandbox/tools)\n   for how the bridge reaches your host across providers (local/Docker vs cloud).\n\n**Client-side and approval-gated tools are not supported** — the harness runs\ntools inside a live process and can't pause across an HTTP round-trip. A tool\nwithout a server `execute()` (or marked `needsApproval`) fails fast; run those\nwith a regular provider adapter.\n\n## Durable runs\n\nA durable sandbox run (you pass `runs` and `durability` to `withSandbox`)\njournals the agent output so a later request can take the run over. ACP does\nnot journal. When durability is wired and you do not set `protocol`, the\nadapter uses `'streaming-json'`.\n\nSet `protocol: 'acp'` only when you want ACP on that call. A fresh ACP run\nwith durability wired logs a warning. An attach against ACP throws\n`DurableAttachNotSupportedError`.\n\n## Headless NDJSON flags\n\nOn the `'streaming-json'` path with auto-approve, the adapter adds\n`--always-approve --no-plan --no-auto-update`. Those flags keep Plan Mode and\nthe CLI update check from blocking a headless run.\n\n## Structured Output\n\nPass `outputSchema` on `chat()`. Grok Build has no native schema flag. The adapter adds the JSON Schema to the prompt (ACP and `streaming-json`) and parses the last assistant text. Tool activity still streams. The object arrives as `structured-output.complete`.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { grokBuildText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\"\nimport { defineSandbox, withSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n})\n\nconst report = await chat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText(\"grok-build\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Review this repo.\" }],\n  outputSchema: Report,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n\nreport.summary\n```\n\nThis path parses JSON from the last assistant message. If extract-only is the job, use `@tanstack/ai-grok`.\n\nOn the client, pass the same schema to `useChat` and read `final`. `partial` stays empty until the end.\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nfunction ReportView() {\n  const { final, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/repo-report\"),\n    outputSchema: Report,\n  })\n\n  if (isLoading) return <p>The agent is inspecting the repo.</p>\n  if (!final) return null\n  return <p>{final.summary}</p>\n}\n```\n\nFull walkthrough, including the client: [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses).\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **Requires a sandbox.** Always run it under `withSandbox(...)`; see the\n  [Sandboxes overview](../sandbox/overview).\n- **Server-only (Node).** The harness spawns the `grok` CLI in a sandbox.\n- **The harness owns the agent loop.** TanStack's agent-loop strategies and\n  per-iteration middleware don't apply inside a harness turn.\n- **No sampling controls.** `temperature`-style options don't exist here.\n- **Cold starts.** Each call runs a full harness turn; expect higher first-token\n  latency than HTTP adapters.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Grok Build\nid: grok-build-adapter\norder: 15\ndescription: \"Use xAI's Grok Build coding agent as a chat backend in TanStack AI — a sandbox harness that runs the grok CLI against a real workspace, with tool bridging via @tanstack/ai-grok-build.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - grok\n  - grok build\n  - xai\n  - harness\n  - agent\n  - coding agent\n  - adapter\n---\n\nThe Grok Build adapter runs xAI's **Grok Build** coding agent as a chat backend.\nUnlike HTTP provider adapters, this is a **harness adapter**: Grok Build runs\nits own agent loop and executes its own tools — shell commands, file edits,\nsearch — by spawning the `grok` CLI **inside a sandbox**. Each `chat()` call runs\none full harness turn; the harness's tool activity streams back as\nalready-resolved tool-call events your UI can render.\n\n> **Requires a sandbox.** `grok-build` declares `requires: [SandboxCapability]`,\n> so `chat()` errors at the call site unless you provide a sandbox with\n> `withSandbox(...)` middleware. The sandbox — your laptop, a Docker container,\n> or a cloud VM — is the filesystem and safety boundary the agent runs in. See\n> the [Sandboxes overview](../sandbox/overview) for the full picture.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nvue: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\npreact: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nangular: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\noctane: @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nYou also need a sandbox provider (e.g. `@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker`) and the\n`grok` CLI available inside the sandbox image.\n\n## Authentication\n\nYour laptop can already have `grok login`. A CI runner only has `XAI_API_KEY`.\nBoth can use the same sandbox provider. The default `authMode` is `'api-key'`.\nSet `'host'` when you want `grok login`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth).\n\n```ts\nimport { grokBuildText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\"\n\ngrokBuildText(\"composer-2.5\")\ngrokBuildText(\"composer-2.5\", { authMode: \"host\" })\n```\n\n- `'api-key'` (default): inject `XAI_API_KEY` and authenticate with it.\n- `'host'`: skip ACP `authenticate`. Use `grok login`. Do not inject\n  `XAI_API_KEY` into that process.\n\nThe two modes list the model under slightly different ids. The adapter maps\nthe short alias for you (see [Models](#models)).\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\nimport { messages, threadId } from './chat-context'\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'grok-build-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n    setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n    secrets: createSecrets({ XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '' }),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  threadId,\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\n## Models\n\nGrok Build accepts any xAI model id its backend supports; the known ids get\nautocomplete (any string is allowed):\n\n| Model id | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| `grok-build` | The short alias. With a grok.com browser login the CLI lists it under this name. |\n| `grok-build-0.1` | The fully-qualified id the CLI lists when authenticated with `XAI_API_KEY`. |\n| `composer-2.5` | Also runnable through the Grok Build harness. |\n\nPass any of these to `grokBuildText(...)` — the adapter resolves `grok-build` to\nthe CLI's `grok-build-0.1` automatically, so the same code works under both auth\nmodes.\n\n## Configuration\n\nAdapter config (second argument to `grokBuildText`):\n\n| Option           | Description                                                                 |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cwd`            | Working directory inside the sandbox. Defaults to `/workspace`.             |\n| `grokExecutable` | Path/name of the `grok` executable inside the sandbox. Defaults to `grok`.  |\n| `env`            | Extra environment variables for the `grok` process inside the sandbox.      |\n| `emitDiff`       | Emit a `file.changed` CUSTOM event with the working-tree `git diff` after the run. Defaults to `true`. |\n| `protocol`       | Harness wire protocol: `'acp'` or `'streaming-json'`. Defaults to `'acp'`. A durable sandbox run with no protocol set uses `'streaming-json'` so the run can journal. |\n| `authMode`       | `'api-key'` (default) uses `XAI_API_KEY`. `'host'` uses `grok login`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth). |\n| `authMethodId`   | Explicit ACP auth method. Wins over `authMode`.                             |\n| `extraArgs`      | Extra raw CLI flags appended verbatim (advanced).                           |\n\nPer-call overrides go through `modelOptions`:\n\n| `modelOptions`  | Description                                                  |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `sessionId`     | Resume an existing Grok Build session (see below).           |\n| `cwd`           | Per-call override of the harness working directory.          |\n| `maxTurns`      | Per-call cap on the number of harness turns.                 |\n| `protocol`      | Per-call override of the harness wire protocol.              |\n| `authMode`      | Per-call `'host'` or `'api-key'`. Default `'api-key'`.       |\n| `authMethodId`  | Per-call ACP auth method. Wins over `authMode`.              |\n\n## Stateful Sessions\n\nGrok Build sessions are stateful — the harness keeps the working context (files\nread, commands run, conclusions reached) between turns. The adapter surfaces the\nsession id of every fresh run as a custom stream event named\n`grok-build.session-id`; thread it back via `modelOptions.sessionId` to resume.\nWhen resuming, only the latest user message is sent — the harness already holds\nthe prior context.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat, chatParamsFromRequest, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const sessionId =\n    typeof params.forwardedProps.sessionId === 'string'\n      ? params.forwardedProps.sessionId\n      : undefined\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n    modelOptions: { sessionId },\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n## Tools\n\nTwo kinds of tools flow through this adapter:\n\n1. **Built-in harness tools** are executed by Grok Build itself (shell, file\n   edits, search) and stream back as tool-call events with results already\n   attached. Your code never executes them.\n2. **Your TanStack tools** are bridged *into* the harness over an authenticated\n   MCP tool-proxy: define them with `toolDefinition().server()` and pass them to\n   `chat({ tools })`. Tool-call events come back under the names you registered.\n   Because the harness runs in a sandbox, see [Sandbox tools](../sandbox/tools)\n   for how the bridge reaches your host across providers (local/Docker vs cloud).\n\n**Client-side and approval-gated tools are not supported** — the harness runs\ntools inside a live process and can't pause across an HTTP round-trip. A tool\nwithout a server `execute()` (or marked `needsApproval`) fails fast; run those\nwith a regular provider adapter.\n\n## Durable runs\n\nA durable sandbox run (you pass `runs` and `durability` to `withSandbox`)\njournals the agent output so a later request can take the run over. ACP does\nnot journal. When durability is wired and you do not set `protocol`, the\nadapter uses `'streaming-json'`.\n\nSet `protocol: 'acp'` only when you want ACP on that call. A fresh ACP run\nwith durability wired logs a warning. An attach against ACP throws\n`DurableAttachNotSupportedError`.\n\n## Headless NDJSON flags\n\nOn the `'streaming-json'` path with auto-approve, the adapter adds\n`--always-approve --no-plan --no-auto-update`. Those flags keep Plan Mode and\nthe CLI update check from blocking a headless run.\n\n## Structured Output\n\nPass `outputSchema` on `chat()`. Grok Build has no native schema flag. The adapter adds the JSON Schema to the prompt (ACP and `streaming-json`) and parses the last assistant text. Tool activity still streams. The object arrives as `structured-output.complete`.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { grokBuildText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\"\nimport { defineSandbox, withSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n})\n\nconst report = await chat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText(\"grok-build\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Review this repo.\" }],\n  outputSchema: Report,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n\nreport.summary\n```\n\nThis path parses JSON from the last assistant message. If extract-only is the job, use `@tanstack/ai-grok`.\n\nOn the client, pass the same schema to `useChat` and read `final`. `partial` stays empty until the end.\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nfunction ReportView() {\n  const { final, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/repo-report\"),\n    outputSchema: Report,\n  })\n\n  if (isLoading) return <p>The agent is inspecting the repo.</p>\n  if (!final) return null\n  return <p>{final.summary}</p>\n}\n```\n\nFull walkthrough, including the client: [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses).\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **Requires a sandbox.** Always run it under `withSandbox(...)`; see the\n  [Sandboxes overview](../sandbox/overview).\n- **Server-only (Node).** The harness spawns the `grok` CLI in a sandbox.\n- **The harness owns the agent loop.** TanStack's agent-loop strategies and\n  per-iteration middleware don't apply inside a harness turn.\n- **No sampling controls.** `temperature`-style options don't exist here.\n- **Cold starts.** Each call runs a full harness turn; expect higher first-token\n  latency than HTTP adapters.\n"}
